'' casetable.tiko -- ustr_casetable.o: the simple case mappings over the BMP.
''
'' GENERATED, AND NOT BY TRANSCRIPTION. Every run below was produced by CALLING
'' fbc's own fb_hUStrToUpper / fb_hUStrToLower once for each of the 65,536 BMP
'' code units and run-length encoding the deltas. Nothing here was copied out of
'' a table by eye, and nothing depends on my having read one correctly:
'' tests/abi/ucase-parity.bas re-asks all 131,072 questions and compares the
'' answers, so the ENCODING is free to differ from fbc's as long as the BEHAVIOUR
'' does not. (It does not differ, as it happens -- 668 + 657 = 1,325 runs, the
'' same count fbc's generated file carries.)
''
'' NOT towupper/towlower. Those are LOCALE-DEPENDENT, so the same ustring would
'' fold differently depending on the user's locale and on which libc the program
'' linked against -- which is the exact platform divergence this type exists to
'' remove. The table is Unicode 15.1.0 simple mappings.
''
'' SIMPLE MAPPINGS ONLY: one unit in, one unit out. Full case mapping can produce
'' more than one character -- German sharp s upper-casing to "SS" is the standard
'' example -- which an in-place unit transform cannot express and which no other
'' FB string type does either.
''
'' SURROGATES ARE LEFT ALONE, deliberately. A lone half has no case, and mapping
'' the two halves of a pair independently would corrupt the character. Case
'' mapping above the BMP is not supported, which is what "simple mapping" means
'' here.

#include once "inc/descriptors.ti"

type TKORT_UCASE_RUN field = 1
	as ushort lo
	as ushort hi
	as long   delta      '' C int32_t -- a delta, not a code unit
end type

